WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.835
You've been hearing a lot about him

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:04.137
because he has been rising in the polls.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.006
And Vivek Ramasamy

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.875
also recently suggested that he wouldn't

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:09.709
have certified

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.578
the election results in the way

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:15.281
that former Vice President Mike Pence did

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.883
Here's what I would have said.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.784
We need single day

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.319
voting on Election Day.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.520
We need paper ballots

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.088
and we need government issued ID

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.523
matching the voter file.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.858
And if we achieve that,

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.860
then we have achieved victory.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.161
And we should not have

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.029
any further complain

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.764
about election integrity in my capacity

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:32.265
as president of the Senate.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.333
I would have led through

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.934
that level of reform

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.603
then on that condition, certify

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.704
the election results,

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.138
served it

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.572
up to the president, President Trump,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.974
then to sign that into law

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.275
and on January 7th,

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.244
declare to the reelection campaign

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.179
pursuant to a free and fair election.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.747
I think that was a missed opportunity

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.216
for those familiar with

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.751
Schoolhouse Rock and separation

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:52.352
of powers.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.220
The vice president has neither

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.822
the authority to send legislation

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.856
directly to Congress,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.525
nor does he have the authority

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.693
to just simply deny election results.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:04.230
But it is notable that since 2022

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.499
and 2022 Vivek Ramaswamy

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.867
seems to disagree

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.470
with 2023 Vivek Ramaswamy.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.571
In his book

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.639
just last year

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.808
he mocked Trump's election lies.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.609
He called his arguments weak

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.378
and he said that reasonable Republicans

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.013
don't believe that the election

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.081
was stolen.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.216
And on the question of the vice

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.717
president specifically,

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.718
he wrote, quote,

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.553
Mike Pence,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.020
the man

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.755
I have great respect for, decided

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.690
it was his constitutional duty

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.425
to resist the president's attempts

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.861
to get him to unilaterally overturn

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.529
the results of the election.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:37.831
He goes on to write,

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:40.800
Our institutions did hold in the end,

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.803
but they shouldn't have been tested Now,

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:44.537
meantime,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.106
that's not the only thing that Ramaswamy

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.040
is getting attention for.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.308
He also has gotten

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.642
quite a bit of backlash

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:50.810
after calling a black

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.212
Democratic congresswoman

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:55.915
a modern grand wizard of the modern KKK.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.750
At a stop in Iowa on Friday,

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.887
Ayanna Pressley, she's

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:01.888
in the Congress today.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:04.157
She's a member of the squad.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.258
Her words, not mine.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.061
We don't want any more black faces

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.597
that don't want to be a black voice.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.767
We don't want any more brown faces

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.370
that don't want to be a brown voice.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.339
Literally word for word.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.473
I'm not putting any dirty words

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.274
in anybody's mouth.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.509
Abraham Kennedy

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.910
wrote the book How to Be an Anti-Racist.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.511
I wrote Woking.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.345
It was a pretty successful

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.280
book, has sold more copies than mine.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.848
Here's what it says.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.450
Opening lines.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.552
The remedy to past discrimination

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.254
is present discrimination.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.321
The remedy to present

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:38.158
discrimination is future discrimination.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.692
So there there's little gaslight

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.793
you when you say this stuff is like,

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.495
oh, you're just making that

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.397
critical race theory. Step up, Neera.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.331
These aren't my words.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.700
These are the words of

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.036
the modern grand wizards

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.605
of the modern KKK.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.375
The man he's talking about there, Ibram

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.876
X Kendi, joins me now.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.045
He's the author of, as Mr.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.046
Ramasamy was saying,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.981
How to Be an Anti-Racist.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.416
And he's also the director

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.184
of the Center

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.685
for Anti-Racist Research

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.554
at Boston University.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.788
Thanks for being here.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.523
I want to get just your reaction

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.659
to what you heard him saying there.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.894
Compare you and Congresswoman Pressley

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:18.298
to the modern grand wizards of the KKK.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:23.870
I just think it's incredibly dangerous.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:27.907
The Ku Klux Klan is is the oldest

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.743
and quite possibly most violent

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.045
white terrorist group,

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.513
really a terrorist, domestic

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.949
terrorist group in American history.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.584
They have engaged

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.551
in generations

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.252
of violence

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.221
against against black people,

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.755
against Jews,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.490
against all sorts of groups.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.025
Stadium agree with.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.560
And they've also

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.330
expressed ideas of of racial hierarchy

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.764
and white supremacy ideas

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:52.432
that are that

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.000
I and Congresswoman

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.668
Pressley have repeatedly

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.303
and constantly challenge.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.638
So it's incredibly dangerous,

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.673
especially in this moment

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:01.674
where, you know,

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.875
all sorts of reports

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.044
point to white supremacists

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.279
as the greatest domestic

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.014
terrorist threat of our time

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.917
to be comparing people to them

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.352
that have spent their lives

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:13.353
challenging them

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.021
and actually who the Klan hates

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.623
because the Klan really doesn't like me.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.192
Look, yesterday

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.994
on CNN's State of the Union, I ran

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.862
a somebody was pressed about this

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.698
and pressed about the violence of the KKK

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.001
and how that could possibly compare

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.002
to anything

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.536
that you or Congresswoman

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.071
Pressley have said.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:32.805
But he said that

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.407
he wanted to provoke a, quote,

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.476
honest discussion in this country.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.479
So just help us here.

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:39.679
I mean,

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.147
what would an honest discussion

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.215
on race

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.683
in this country in this moment

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.652
actually look like?

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.655
Well, I think we would start

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.090
with racial disparities and inequities.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.626
We would identify the evidence

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.128
that points to, for instance,

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:55.528
let's say

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:55.795
black

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:56.829
people are more likely

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:59.699
to be impoverished or incarcerated

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.167
or killed by police

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.936
or dying of heart disease and cancer.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.407
And we would also recognize that there's

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.908
nothing inferior

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.743
about black people as a group.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:11.377
So there must

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.112
be policies and practices

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.114
that are leading to those disparities.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.149
And as American

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.617
as we should come together

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:18.418
to identify

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:18.951
and eliminate

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.886
those disparities,

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.688
that's an honest conversation

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.989
based on evidence

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.358
and based on notions of racial equality.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:27.660
There's a difference of opinion,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.561
I think, here

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.563
between you and Ramos for me about

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.199
whether it requires actively

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.002
addressing racial wrongs in

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.671
order to to address them in the future.

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.374
But that kind of rhetoric from him

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.342
doesn't seem to be

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:43.843
part of that conversation.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:44.777
I do wonder, though,

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.312
I mean, this is happening on the campaign

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.547
trail, right?

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:50.483
He's one of several candidates of color

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:51.951
in the Republican race,

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.853
but he's doing really well

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.988
and is making these arguments

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:57.557
at a particular moment

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:59.025
for him in this race.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:05:59.726
Why do you.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.160
Do you think that this is a part

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.663
of why he is doing so well right now?

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.367
Without question.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:10.036
And unfortunately, you have

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:12.305
too many candidates,

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:14.207
particularly Republican candidates

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.174
of color

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.310
who recognize that one of the ways

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:17.810
in which

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.345
they can sort of boost

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.481
their political appeal to right.

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:23.616
Republicans is by telling them

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.385
that they are not racist

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:26.919
and then turning around

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:30.123
and attacking those who are pointing out

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.392
racism as the real problem,

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.693
as the real racist.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:35.661
And you know, we've seen candidate

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.930
after candidate be boosted,

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.932
particularly candidates of color,

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.034
by by essentially feeding

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.137
white Republicans their denial.

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:46.239
And that's all Vivek is doing.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:47.073
He knows that.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:50.843
And the irony is that is based on racism

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:53.479
and it's based on his skin color.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.514
At the same time,

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.249
he's claiming racism is

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:57.183
no longer an issue.

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:58.718
Ever.

00:06:58.718 --> 00:06:59.552
Max Kennedy, thank you

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.553
for joining us tonight

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:03.756
and responding directly to all of that.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.557
Thank you for having me.

